<section class="section architecture-section" id="architecture" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
  <div class="page-container">
    <div class="section-heading arch-heading">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="section-index">02</span> &nbsp; / &nbsp; THE ARCHITECTURE</div>
        <h2 id="architecture-title">One language.<br/><em>One resolved plan.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>The interesting work happens before source compilation. Package registrations become a typed, deterministic configuration for a language implementation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="explorer" data-lifecycle>
      <div class="explorer-head">
        <div class="explorer-title"><span class="explorer-cursor" aria-hidden="true">●</span> LIFECYCLE EXPLORER</div>
        <span class="explorer-hint">SELECT A STAGE TO INSPECT <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="explorer-grid">
        <div class="explorer-steps" role="group" aria-label="Language configuration stages">
          <button type="button" class="explorer-step is-selected" data-step-button="definition" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span><strong>LanguageDefinition</strong><span class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
          <button type="button" class="explorer-step" data-step-button="compiler" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span><strong>LanguageCompiler</strong><span class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
          <button type="button" class="explorer-step" data-step-button="plan" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span><strong>LanguagePlan</strong><span class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
          <button type="button" class="explorer-step" data-step-button="runtime" aria-pressed="false"><span>04</span><strong>LanguageRuntime</strong><span class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
          <div class="explorer-aside"><span class="kicker">THE DISTINCTION</span><p>These are stages of <b>language configuration</b> — not four passes over a user's source file.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="explorer-display" aria-live="polite">
          <div class="display-top"><span>LANGUAGE / CONFIGURATION TIME</span><span>MODEL 01—04</span></div>
          <div class="display-stage" data-step-panel="definition">
            <div class="display-serial">01 / DECLARE</div>
            <h3>Choose what belongs.</h3>
            <p>Describe the language, select features and backends, and provide package-owned registrations. No source code is parsed here.</p>
            <div class="display-code"><span>use feature</span> <strong>acme.pricing.core</strong><br/><span>enable</span> <strong>interpreter, compiled</strong><br/><span>policy</span> <strong>RequireDeterminism</strong></div>
            <div class="display-footnote">Source: LanguageDefinitionBuilder / Acme sample</div>
          </div>
          <div class="display-stage" data-step-panel="compiler" hidden>
            <div class="display-serial">02 / RESOLVE</div>
            <h3>Let the planner decide.</h3>
            <p>LanguageCompiler resolves declared dependencies, conflicts, ownership constraints and type-compatible routes. Ambiguity can be diagnosed instead of silently guessed away.</p>
            <div class="display-visual">
              <span class="display-node">Packages</span><span class="display-arrow">→</span><span class="display-node node-strong">Typed resolution</span><span class="display-arrow">→</span><span class="display-node">Diagnostics / plan</span>
            </div>
            <div class="display-footnote">Deterministic planning; no semantic optimizer proof</div>
          </div>
          <div class="display-stage" data-step-panel="plan" hidden>
            <div class="display-serial">03 / FREEZE</div>
            <h3>The selection becomes a contract.</h3>
            <p>An immutable LanguagePlan records selected contributions, ordering, typed routes and package identity. Runtime does not re-plan behind your back.</p>
            <div class="display-code"><span>PLAN</span> <strong>immutable</strong><br/><span>ROUTES</span> <strong>typed &amp; selected</strong><br/><span>PROVENANCE</span> <strong>package identity</strong></div>
            <div class="display-footnote">The plan is structural evidence, not a correctness certificate</div>
          </div>
          <div class="display-stage" data-step-panel="runtime" hidden>
            <div class="display-serial">04 / MATERIALIZE</div>
            <h3>Run only what was selected.</h3>
            <p>LanguageRuntime checks package provenance and binds the exact chosen components. The application's input artifact can then follow a planned backend route.</p>
            <div class="display-visual">
              <span class="display-node node-strong">LanguagePlan</span><span class="display-arrow">→</span><span class="display-node">Exact components</span><span class="display-arrow">→</span><span class="display-node">Backend</span>
            </div>
            <div class="display-footnote">Host applications still own isolation and trust policy</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="two-clocks">
      <div class="clock-label"><span class="section-index">≠</span><h3>Two different clocks.</h3><p>Framework composition is not the same operation as compiling a source program.</p></div>
      <div class="clock-routes">
        <div class="clock-route">
          <span>CONFIGURATION TIME</span>
          <div>Packages <b>→</b> Definition <b>→</b> Compiler <b>→</b> Plan <b>→</b> Runtime</div>
        </div>
        <div class="clock-route">
          <span>PROGRAM TIME</span>
          <div>Input artifact <b>→</b> planned typed route <b>→</b> chosen executor</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
